# EC2 Module

This Terraform module creates and manages an Amazon EC2 instance using reusable,
environment-independent infrastructure patterns.

## Responsibilities

The module is responsible for:

- Creating an EC2 instance.
- Attaching the supplied subnet.
- Attaching supplied security groups.
- Attaching an IAM instance profile.
- Configuring the root EBS volume.
- Enabling EBS encryption.
- Optionally using a customer-managed KMS key.
- Enforcing IMDSv2 by default.
- Configuring detailed monitoring.
- Supporting optional user data.
- Applying standardized resource tags.

The module does not create or manage:

- VPCs
- Subnets
- Security groups
- IAM roles
- IAM instance profiles
- Launch templates
- Auto Scaling groups
- Load balancers

Those responsibilities belong to their respective modules.

## Architecture

The EC2 module consumes resources created by other modules:

    VPC
     |
     +-- Subnet ID
     |
    Security Groups
     |
     +-- Security Group IDs
     |
    IAM
     |
     +-- Instance Profile
     |
    KMS
     |
     +-- KMS Key ID/ARN
     |
     v
    EC2 Module
     |
     v
    EC2 Instance

The environment layer is responsible for connecting these modules.

## Multiple EC2 Instances

The module creates one EC2 instance per module instance.

Multiple EC2 instances should be created from the environment using
`for_each` rather than duplicating the EC2 implementation inside the module.

Example:

```hcl
module "ec2" {
  source = "../../modules/EC2"

  for_each = var.ec2_instances

  name                      = each.value.name
  ami_id                    = each.value.ami_id
  instance_type             = each.value.instance_type
  subnet_id                 = each.value.subnet_id
  security_group_ids        = each.value.security_group_ids
  iam_instance_profile_name = each.value.iam_instance_profile_name

  root_volume_size      = each.value.root_volume_size
  root_volume_type      = each.value.root_volume_type
  root_volume_encrypted = each.value.root_volume_encrypted
  root_volume_kms_key_id = each.value.root_volume_kms_key_id

  enable_detailed_monitoring = each.value.enable_detailed_monitoring

  user_data = each.value.user_data

  instance_initiated_shutdown_behavior = (
    each.value.instance_initiated_shutdown_behavior
  )

  common_tags = var.common_tags
}